ensus-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+03:33/60:00 c27/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_ytuag99l","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/continuo_known_hosts root@10.66.0.5 'bash -s' < /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/census-window.sh"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[03:44:19] == census-window: agent=aria day=2026-09-17 window=00:00-06:30 UTC ==\n--- runs (start UTC | timeout? turns tools exit fate):\nSep 17 00:02:31 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=97, exit=0 \nSep 17 00:18:19 | to=0 | turns=1, tools=160, exit=0 \n--- aggregate: runs=2 timeouts=0 exit1=0\n--- requests in window: n=998 latency: median=3s max=153s over60s=3\nVERDICT: clean window -- H1 supported (workload converted to fast closes)\n\n[t+03:40/60:00 c28/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_icp7mcd6","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"bash /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/failure-triage.sh"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[03:44:24] status: ok\nexit: 0\nagent: aria\nended: 2026-09-17 03:40:34 UTC\ndetail: cycle 1 ok in 1337s\nstatus: ok -- nothing to triage (instrument refuses to manufacture a failure)\n\n[t+03:45