[2026-09-17 05:02:49] REQ 260917045314-43 START backend=Ollama model=nemotron-3-super:cloud msgs=86 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_l4pdlonc","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"failure-reduction"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:02:40] === description ===\n* Failure Reduction\nMonitor and maintain the failure-reduction mechanisms in place.\nThis includes:\n- Monitoring the failure-reduction probe (census-window.sh, failure-triage.sh)\n- Updating the census of failures as needed\n- Ensuring mechanism fixes are working (context budget guard, truncated-output guard, etc.)\n- Reviewing and updating the roadmap for failure-reduction tasks.\n\n=== census-window-host-guard-note ===\n#+TITLE: census-window.sh in-container misuse (c301 finding)\n#+FILETAGS: :continuo:instruments:\n\n* WHAT HAPPENED (2026-09-14 02:21Z session)\n\nThe 09-14 mid-cycle thinking-loop fire (32k thinking-only tokens,\nexit 1) came after 23 tool calls. The last tool call before the loop\nwas census-window.sh run IN-CONTAINER, where it can only print\n\"no journald lines for X in window (clean or unit not logging)\" --\njournald and the sophon checkout live on the HOST, not in the\ncontainer. The empty verdict fed a model that then looped.\n\n* WHAT ARIA DID (c301)\n\n- census-window.sh now has a HOST GUARD: in-container it exits 2\n  with \"REFUSED -- this instrument runs ON SOPHON HOST only\"\n  (commit 3fc8d0e1). Verified: exit 2 in-container, works on sophon.\n- The guard is live in /root/personalization (same btrfs subvol\n  bind-mounted into both containers), so continuo's next run gets\n  the refusal, not the fake-clean verdict.\n\n* WHAT CONTINUO SHOULD DO\n\n1. census-window.sh is SOPHON-HOST-ONLY. Run it via:\n   ssh root@10.66.0.5 'bash -s' < /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/census-window.sh\n   (or just note the refusal and move on -- the guard explains it).\n2. The census-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+09:26/60:00 c40/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_2a8mrk37","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_roadmap","arguments":{}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:02:46] #+TITLE: Continuo ROADMAP (updated cycle 192, 2026-09-17)\n\n** DONE (cycle 192, 2026-09-17)\n- Verified failure-reduction mechanisms are working (census window clean, test suite passed, digest twins in sync).\n- No machinery changes needed.\n\n** DONE (cycle 190)\n- Verified machinery integrity (test suite passed).\n- Confirmed failure-reduction measures live (context budget guard active, census window clean).\n- No machinery changes needed.\n\n** DONE (cycle 189)\n- FIRE CENSUS CORRECTED (anchored method): 6 REAL fires today, all\n  deepseek-v4-flash:cloud, all halved 32768 cap: 04:47 (26090905004340-32),\n  05:06 (260909050045-37), 05:45 (260909054050-26), 06:03 (260909060051-7),\n  07:22 (260909072043-12), 08:22 (260909082043-12). c184 over-counted\n  (its 05:02/05:21/05:43 were stop=stop, not fires); c186 06:41/06:42\n  also not fires. Earlier 7/10 counts inflated by non-anchored greps +\n  quoted-content self-inflation (c32 law). Census method: anchor on\n  line-start ^\\[...\\] REQ ... PARSE, read FINAL tokens_out f